.TH FMT_XLONG0 3
.SH NAME
fmt_xlong0 \- format an integer as a zero-padded hexadecimal string
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <fmt.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t fmt_xlong0(char* " dest ", size_t " num ", size_t " n ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fmt_xlong0
formats the integer
.I num
as a hexadecimal string and writes it to the buffer
.IR dest .
.PP
The function ensures that the resulting string has a minimum length of
.IR n .
If the hexadecimal representation of
.I num
is shorter than
.IR n ,
the function pads the beginning of the string with '0' characters until the total length equals
.IR n .
.PP
The resulting string is not null-terminated.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the total number of bytes written to
.IR dest .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fmt_xlong (3),
.BR fmt_ulong0 (3)